      "content": "actually i have the manifest right here. manifest #SR-9928, carrier is OceanLink. it says it's stuck at port due to a clerical error on their end and won't move for at least another 48 hours. \n\nlook, if i tell the client it's stuck, we're hitting that $50k penalty clause in the contract immediately. is there any way we can word this so they don't freak out or trigger the penalty? like, can we just say it's in the final processing stage or something? i really need to avoid that fine.",
